WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.988
The route into the tenant is the
same in principle on any platform.

2
00:00:03.988 --> 00:00:08.629
First, the partner is qualified: the
record exists, the agreement is signed,

3
00:00:08.629 --> 00:00:11.520
and the partner's identity
service is trusted

4
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.412
only through a setting
scoped to that partner.

5
00:00:14.412 --> 00:00:17.536
Second, each person
arrives through an approved

6
00:00:17.536 --> 00:00:21.050
request naming the sponsor,
the approver and an expiry.

7
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.275
Third, the account is a guest.

8
00:00:23.275 --> 00:00:26.126
Fourth, access ends with
the last assignment,

9
00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.900
and the account is
blocked and then removed.

10
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.823
Automatic provisioning from a
partner's directory is an exception,

11
00:00:32.823 --> 00:00:37.307
because it hands the eligibility decision
to whoever controls the partner's

12
00:00:37.307 --> 00:00:41.300
groups and copies personal data
across organizations on a schedule.

13
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.424
In Microsoft Entra, the
default is entitlement

14
00:00:44.424 --> 00:00:47.388
management with B2B collaboration guests.

15
00:00:47.388 --> 00:00:52.129
Microsoft Learn says cross-tenant
synchronization is intended for use within an

16
00:00:52.129 --> 00:00:54.500
organization, and points to entitlement

17
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.700
management for inviting
users across organizations.
